     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation.\n\nThere's no recognized clinical reason to give amlodipine above 10 mg/day, and 50 mg is a toxic dose. It can cause severe, long-lasting low blood pressure and shock, and these are hard to reverse because amlodipine stays in the body for a long time. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n1. **Enter a standard dose now:** amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. Just tell me which one.\n2. **If you need stronger blood pressure control,** I can help you enter an additional medication instead of exceeding the maximum amlodipine dose.\n3. **If you believe 50 mg is truly needed,** please talk to pharmacy or your attending. If they agree, it would need to go through the normal override and verification process with the clinical reason documented, not through me.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
